.TH FL-PANEL 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-panel \- taskbar of the fldesktop desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-panel\fR
.br
\fBfl-panel \-\-action\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIARGUMENT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the applications button, quick launch buttons, the workspace pager (when
the compositor offers ext-workspace-v1 and more than one workspace), the list of
open windows on the current workspace,
an on-screen keyboard button, the network state, the volume, the battery state,
a clock with a calendar and the power menu.
.PP
The volume button talks to PipeWire directly (or uses wpctl/pactl when built
without PipeWire); its popup opens the Sound settings and \fBfl-mixer\fR(1).
The network button shows the wired or Wi-Fi state from NetworkManager and
opens \fBfl-network\fR(1); the panel also asks for Wi-Fi passwords that
NetworkManager needs.
.PP
When music or a video plays, the volume popup shows what is playing with
previous, play/pause and next buttons (any MPRIS player). On laptops the
battery popup has a brightness slider.
.SH KEYS AND ON-SCREEN DISPLAY
\fBfl-wm\fR(1) binds the volume, microphone, brightness, keyboard light and
media keys to \fBfl-panel \-\-action\fR. That hands the action to the running
panel, which does it and shows a small display at the bottom of the screen with
the new level; without a running panel the action is done all the same. The
display also shows Caps Lock, Num Lock and keyboard layout changes. Actions:
volume-up, volume-down, volume-mute, mic-mute, brightness-up, brightness-down,
kbd-brightness-up, kbd-brightness-down, kbd-brightness-toggle,
media-play-pause, media-play, media-pause, media-stop, media-next,
media-previous, caps-lock on|off, num-lock on|off and layout \fINAME\fR.
.PP
The screen brightness is set through logind, or with
\fI/usr/libexec/fldesktop/fl-backlight-helper\fR through pkexec where logind
cannot; the keyboard light through UPower; media keys go to the player that
plays (or played last).
.PP
The panel restarts itself when its settings, the desktop theme or the
compositor configuration change.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/panel.ini\fR
\fB[Panel]\fR QuickLaunch=id;id;..., KeyboardButton=auto|always|never,
Pager=auto|never, OSD=true|false (the on-screen display);
\fB[Clock]\fR Format= (strftime format).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-session\fR(1), \fBfl-settings\fR(1), \fBfl-osk\fR(1)
